    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Mullery O’Gara are delighted to present 25 Harmony Avenue, a charming two-bedroom red brick period home tucked away in this highly regarded residential setting in the heart of Donnybrook. Originally commissioned in 1914 by Pembroke Urban District Council, the homes on Harmony Avenue were designed by prominent Dublin architect George Luke O’Connor as working-class cottages. Today, the terrace retains its distinctive period character while offering comfortable and well-proportioned accommodation.\r\n\r\nOn entering, the entrance hall leads into the main living room, which features solid hardwood flooring, dark-toned finishes, attractive built-in shelving and a gas-fired fireplace, with gas-fired central heating providing further comfort. The kitchen is situated to the rear and is well equipped with Neff appliances including oven, hob and extractor fan, together with shaker-style units and excellent storage.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation continues to the rear with a practical laundry cupboard incorporating the washing machine, boiler and water tank, while the modern bathroom features a walk-in shower, WC and contemporary glass bowl sink. There is access to a private rear decking area, providing a pleasant outdoor space.\r\n\r\nUpstairs are two generously proportioned double bedrooms, both with built-in wardrobes. The master bedroom also features a large glazed door onto the existing roof. Several neighbouring properties have extended upwards, highlighting potential to do the same, subject to planning permission.\r\n\r\nThe location is a particular feature of this property. Harmony Avenue is set just off Brookvale Road in a quiet and established residential enclave, while remaining within easy reach of Donnybrook Village and Eglinton Road. The surrounding area offers an excellent selection of cafés, shops and everyday amenities, together with a superb choice of highly regarded schools. The River Dodder and its riverside walks are also close by with Herbert Park, the RDS, Ballsbridge and the city centre all readily accessible. The area is exceptionally well served by public transport and is within easy reach of Dublin’s main business districts.\r\n\r\n25 Harmony Avenue represents an excellent opportunity to acquire a characterful period home in one of Dublin 4’s most sought-after residential locations."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Downstairs\r\nEntrance Hall\r\nSolid hardwood flooring. Mat well.\r\nLiving Room\r\nSolid hardwood flooring, tv corner unit with shelving, White stone fireplace surround with polished black granite hearth and traditional cast-iron gas-fired fireplace insert. White corner shelving unit featuring a lower storage cabinet. Under-stairs storage.\r\nKitchen\r\nShaker-style units, Neff appliances including gas hob. Tiled Splashback. Radiator and Gas Boiler.\r\nLaundry Cupboard\r\nWashing machine, hot water tank.\r\nBathroom\r\nFully Tiled, Walk-in shower, WC and glass bowl sink with mirror. Radiator\r\nRear Decking\r\nPrivate rear decking area.\r\nUpstairs\r\nBedroom 1 – Master Bedroom\r\nDouble bedroom with original fireplace and built in wardrobe with mirror front and radiator. Large glass door. \r\nBedroom 2\r\nGood-sized double bedroom with built-in storage and radiator."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
